WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:10.080
My connection to the sea started when I was little I spent 
most of my summers at the sea. Swimming, snorkelling… 

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:19.190
Ever since I was two and a half years old, I started swimming, I kept on developing love for the water 

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.190
The water here in Moraska is different from anywhere else here in Slovenia 

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.190
As a Slovenian I feel like water is part of my DNA

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.050
the part of the country where I am from is surrounded by

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.150
lakes and rivers and waterfalls and

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.050
there is something so healing about water. I love, I love the sound of it

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.080
it kind of puts me into a meditative place.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.220
Despite being so small Slovenia really holds high biodiversity  

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.150
but also diversity of geomorphological forms and also types of water,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.150
we have these lively Alpine rivers flowing down the mountains and meeting 

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.200
the sea, the Adriatic Sea, and bringing in nutrients, minerals

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.210
that support high-productivity and diversity. 

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.020
This place is special because it’s like a perfect union of man and nature

00:01:25.021 --> 00:01:30.050
very contemplative and good for humans and animal and plants living here.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:35.010
You would not think at first sight but also the mud here is good for us

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.090
putting it on, feeling how it works on the skin, it’s amazing.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:45.170
In the same way as the landscape, the land, and the waters change along the Slovenian coast,

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.000
so 5 mins from place to place the mud can be completely different. 

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.210
Lake Bohinj is really special, it’s the biggest permanent lake in Slovenia

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.230
and it’s also a lot quieter than the other lakes which makes it that much nicer to be in. 

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:07.010
What makes me most happy though, is that this beautiful nature is only

00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:13.190
one hour away from our very busy city, Ljubljana, so that makes it extra special.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.230
One of the things I love the most is how I can fill my water bottle up

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:24.170
whether there is tap water or going by the mountain where there is the water source. 

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:30.150
Water in Slovenia tastes different wherever you go and one such a area is Rogaska

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.180
where water is full of magnesium and it’s very beneficial for your health.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.060
In Slovenia we have two waters which are very special because 

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.120
they are mineral drinking waters,

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:46.020
all other waters are thermal mineral waters which are used for the Balneo therapies

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.120
but here the Balneo therapy means drinking.

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:54.130
Donat Ng mineral water has been attracting people here for centuries

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:59.160
because it is the mineral water with the highest content of magnesium, no other water

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:06.190
in the world has more than 1000, to be exact 1040 milligrams, of magnesium in 1 litre.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:16.080
The black mineral water comes from deep underground in Zara Mulabasin,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.120
They call it black gold because of a high concentration

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:25.140
of healing substances and it has beneficial effects on health.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.170
I prescribe patients a program:

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.150
In the morning patients might have bathing in water

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:38.000
and in the afternoon they can have a mud treatment.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:47.000
One of my favourite places to escape to is a very magical natural pool surrounded

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:52.130
by beautiful waterfalls, but I am not going to tell you exactly where that is, 

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:57.100
you're going to have to come and discover it yourself.

